From 9f855e59a323377cf4609cb0d5377b9185ebb5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Esposito <matthew.esposito@nordicsemi.no>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:54:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] zchunk_range: coalesce adjacent chunks up to max-ranges

range_add() raises range->count for every chunk and lets
range_merge_combined() collapse the new range into the previous one when
they are adjacent. The merge can only take place when the next chunk is
added, so checking the counter after range_add() checks it one chunk too
early: the loop stops as soon as count reaches max_ranges, even if the
chunks that follow would have been merged into the last range instead of
opening a new one.

Consequences are that the last range of each request is cut at the chunk
that reached the limit, and that with "max-ranges = 1" a merge can never
happen at all: every missing chunk is asked with its own HTTP request,
even when hundreds of them are consecutive in the ZCK file. And 1 is the
value that must be set when the server accepts a single range only, as
it is the case with AWS S3 or some CDNs.

Check the limit before adding the chunk and stop only if the chunk does
not continue the last range, that means only if a new range must really
be opened.

Test with a ZCK file of 20 chunks where 9 chunks are missing, grouped in
4 consecutive runs:

                    before    after
    max-ranges 1    9 req.    4 req.
    max-ranges 2    3 req.    2 req.
    max-ranges 150  1 req.    1 req.

The requested bytes do not change, no request contains more ranges than
max-ranges, and each call still returns at least one chunk so that the
handler always makes progress.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Esposito <matthew.esposito@nordicsemi.no>

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to the swupdate mailing list]
---
diff --git a/handlers/zchunk_range.c b/handlers/zchunk_range.c
index 2b24d0b2..69e2d1fa 100644
--- a/handlers/zchunk_range.c
+++ b/handlers/zchunk_range.c
@@ -168,14 +168,16 @@ zck_range *zchunk_get_missing_range(zckCtx *zck, zckChunk *first, int max_ranges
 	}
 
 	for(zckChunk *chk = first ? first : zck_get_first_chunk(zck); chk; chk = zck_get_next_chunk(chk)) {
-		if (zck_get_chunk_valid(chk))
+		if (zck_get_chunk_valid(chk)) {
+			/* the next missing chunk cannot be merged, it opens a new range */
+			if (max_ranges >= 0 && range->count >= max_ranges)
+				break;
 			continue;
-		if(!range_add(range, chk)) {
+		}
+		if (!range_add(range, chk)) {
 			zchunk_range_free(&range);
 			return NULL;
 		}
-		if(max_ranges >= 0 && range->count >= max_ranges)
-			break;
 	}
 	return range;
 }
